error[E0205]: cannot assign to `it`, it is immutable
  --> tests/errors/E0205_copy_of_element.al:11:5
   |
11 |     it.qty += 1;
   |     ^^
  = hint: `it` is a copy of `items[0]`; to change `items[0]` itself, write `items[0].qty` instead of `it.qty` (declaring `it` with `var` would change only the copy)

error[E0205]: `it` is immutable and cannot be passed as `mut`
  --> tests/errors/E0205_copy_of_element.al:12:14
   |
12 |     push(mut it.tags, "sale");
   |              ^^
  = hint: `it` is a copy of `items[0]`; to change `items[0]` itself, write `items[0].tags` instead of `it.tags` (declaring `it` with `var` would change only the copy)

error[E0205]: cannot assign to `n`, it is immutable
  --> tests/errors/E0205_copy_of_element.al:14:5
